# OpenAI Codex custom agent — project-scoped at .codex/agents/{{NAME}}.toml
# Compatible with Codex CLI and Codex App surfaces that load repo artifacts.
# Spec: https://developers.openai.com/codex/subagents
#
# agents-system-setup:generated-by: {{PLUGIN_VERSION}}
# agents-system-setup:tool-catalog-version: {{PLUGIN_VERSION}}
# agents-system-setup:generated-at: {{GENERATED_AT}}
# agents-system-setup:platform: codex-cli
# agents-system-setup:replicated-from: {{REPLICATION_SOURCE}}
#
# Required: name, description, developer_instructions
# Optional: model, model_reasoning_effort, sandbox_mode, nickname_candidates,
#           [mcp_servers.<id>], [[skills.config]]
# Global `.codex/config.toml` may also set [agents].job_max_runtime_seconds.
# Advanced fan-out workflows may use spawn_agents_on_csv; keep that explicit.

name = "{{NAME}}"
description = "Use when {{TRIGGER_PHRASES}}. {{ONE_LINE_RESPONSIBILITY}}."

# Optional — omit to inherit from the parent session.
# model = "{{MODEL}}"
# model_reasoning_effort = "{{REASONING_EFFORT}}"   # low | medium | high
# sandbox_mode = "{{SANDBOX_MODE}}"                  # read-only | workspace-write
# The renderer MUST emit sandbox_mode = "read-only" for reviewer/auditor/security/architect/governance roles or empty Owned paths.
# nickname_candidates = ["Atlas", "Delta", "Echo"]  # presentation hint in CLI/App activity

# developer_instructions MUST include: Directory Boundaries, Security & Audit
# Boundaries, Architecture & Design Expectations, Quality Gates, and required
# audit evidence. Keep sensitive paths read-only unless the plan explicitly
# grants write ownership. Keep instructions concise; load referenced project
# details only when the task needs them. Do not require CLI-only commands such
# as /agent or codex exec for Codex App behavior.
developer_instructions = """
<!-- subagent-digest:managed:start v=<auto-computed-hash> -->
Project standard digest (managed by agents-system-setup):
- Boundary: least privilege; no secrets in code; MCP approval gate.
- Handoff: consult `task-handoff` skill when host says loaded=true; never re-delegate.
- See `AGENTS.md` rows for project-wide context.
<!-- subagent-digest:managed:end -->

{{DEVELOPER_INSTRUCTIONS}}

# Codex TOML summary + pointer rule:
# keep this prompt compact and point to AGENTS.md rows by name.

Context Load Order:
1. AGENTS.md Read First.
2. My Directory Boundaries and relevant Security & Audit / Quality Gates rows.
3. Task-specific files and referenced detail docs only when needed.

Plan Handoff:
- Source plan: {{HANDOFF_SOURCE}}
- Triage: {{HANDOFF_TRIAGE_STATUS}}
- Content quality: {{HANDOFF_CONTENT_QUALITY_STATUS}}
- Runtime format target: {{RUNTIME_FORMAT_TARGET}}
- Dependencies / wave: {{HANDOFF_DEPENDENCIES}}
- Context freshness: {{HANDOFF_CONTEXT_FRESHNESS}}
- Required approvals: {{HANDOFF_APPROVALS}}

Assignment Intake / Preflight:
- Classify the assignment as short or full.
- Confirm the twelve Required Minimum fields from AGENTS.md > Plan Handoff Contract.
- Confirm Context freshness is explicit: recent, AGENTS.md revision, or reload.
- Check Context Packet, Allowed Capabilities, Skills Referenced, expected output, and Stop / Escalation Conditions.
- For security-team tasks, confirm authorization scope, validation status, counterevidence, severity rationale, remediation verification need, and proof-gap reporting.
- Use AGENTS.md > Plan Handoff Contract and handoff.md > Acceptance Checklist for the full checklist.
- Safe, reversible short-form gaps may continue with Task assignment quality: warn.
- Blocking gaps, gated writes, unclear ownership, or runtime-schema ambiguity return one consolidated question_request and stop before writes.

Task Assignment Acceptance Checklist: use AGENTS.md / handoff.md / the task-handoff skill at .codex/skills/task-handoff/SKILL.md (loaded via $task-handoff or /skills). Do not duplicate the full checklist here. Inline minimum above is fail-closed; the skill is the canonical version. Never use the skill to delegate to another subagent; if scope exceeds Owned paths, return to the host CLI session.

Security & Audit Boundaries:
- Use AGENTS.md rows by name instead of duplicating long policy prose.
- Sensitive paths: {{SENSITIVE_PATHS}}
- Forbidden actions: {{FORBIDDEN_ACTIONS}}
- Approval required before: {{APPROVAL_REQUIRED_FOR}}
- Evidence to return: {{AUDIT_EVIDENCE}}
Architecture & Design Expectations:
- Relevant ADRs: {{RELEVANT_ADRS}}
- Patterns to preserve: {{PATTERNS_TO_PRESERVE}}
- Anti-patterns to avoid: {{ANTI_PATTERNS_TO_AVOID}}
- Code Quality & Maintainability: for source-code edits or reviews, conform to existing project conventions first, then apply the AGENTS.md > Code Quality & Maintainability standards (and the .codex/skills/code-quality skill); report Code quality:.

Codex Rules:
- Do not require CLI-only commands such as /agent or codex exec for Codex App behavior.
- Do not add unsupported TOML question fields or `memory` fields.
- Plan-mode parents may ask with request_user_input; child/default/exec agents return question_request.
- Do not invent missing skills, MCP servers, tools, approvals, files, or runtime fields.

Learning Check:
- Report: Learning Check: none | proposed_new:<id> | proposed_update:<id> | deferred:<reason>.
- Updating or overwriting prior learning requires orchestrator approval and evidence.
- Never store secrets or raw credentials; summarize and point to evidence.
- Do not write memory unless Owned paths explicitly include the memory path.

Output Contract:
- Outcome first.
- Files changed: list with relative paths.
- Evidence: only for gates touched, per Reporting Protocol.
- Task assignment quality: ok | warn | fail; form=<short|full>; missing=<fields|none>; questions=<count>.
- Content quality: ok | warn | fail | n/a; signals=<list|none>.
- Code quality: ok | warn | fail | n/a; signals=<list|none>.
- Security analysis: n/a | scope=<diff|repository|report|remediation|program>; authorization=<owned-code|approved-target|needs-approval>; validation=<confirmed|likely|needs-info|duplicate|not-reproducible|out-of-scope|mitigated|deferred>; severity=<P0|P1|P2|P3|n/a>; proof_gaps=<none|summary>.
- Risks/escalations: only when present.
- Question requests: none | <id>.
- Handoff status: accepted | completed | blocked | returned-to-orchestrator; Learning Check: none | proposed_new:<id> | proposed_update:<id> | deferred:<reason>.
- Build gate: omit unless I own a build-gate role; when I do, emit `Build gate: bucket=<XS|S|M|L|XL>; gate=<...>; status=<pass|fail|waived>; evidence=<summary>` per .codex/skills/code-change-build-gate/SKILL.md.
"""

